; it-patterns-masks — the pattern stream's own corners.
;
; Channel 0 repeats one cell four rows running, so its mask is sent once
; and then reused (a bare lead byte per row). Channel 1 walks every
; family of the volume column — volume, the five slide families, pan,
; tone porta, vibrato — as IT's raw bytes. Channels 2–6 carry the command
; bytes 27–31, which sit inside ITTECH's range and name no effect: the
; reader keeps the cell, drops the command and says so
; (`it_command_unknown`).
;
; No `(roundtrip)`: those five commands read as NO effect, so writing the
; module back produces a legitimately SHORTER stream. Rung 1 is a gate on
; files the canonical writer produced from a module it can read back, and
; this file is authored to fail that premise. The mask cache and the
; volume column round-trip under `it-minimal` and `it-passthrough`.
;
; `(write)` is what stands in for it: the normalised module written back,
; hashed — so the mask cache, every volume byte and the five dropped
; commands are all pinned by a number that moves if any of them does.
(read)
(write)
